## 3. Video Feed UX (The Core Experience)

### Full-Screen Immersive Feed
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — Full viewport video container
<div className="h-dvh w-full snap-start relative">
  <VideoPlayer src={video.url} />
  <ActionBar className="absolute right-3 bottom-24" />
  <VideoInfo className="absolute left-3 bottom-6" />
</div>
```

**Rules:**
- Each video occupies **100dvh** (dynamic viewport height) — accounts for mobile browser chrome.
- Use `scroll-snap-type: y mandatory` for precise snap-to-video scrolling.
- Action bar (like, comment, share, bookmark) is positioned on the right side, vertically stacked.
- Video metadata (username, caption, music) is overlaid on the bottom-left with gradient background.

### Auto-Play & Pause
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — IntersectionObserver for visibility-based playback
const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
  ([entry]) => {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
      videoRef.current?.play()
    } else {
      videoRef.current?.pause()
    }
  },
  { threshold: 0.6 }  // Play when 60%+ visible
)
```

**Rules:**
- Videos MUST auto-play when scrolled into view and auto-pause when scrolled away.
- Use `IntersectionObserver` with a threshold of 0.5–0.7.
- Only ONE video should be playing at any time. Pause all others.
- Support tap-to-pause/play gesture on the video itself.
- Mute by default on first visit (browser autoplay policy). Show a clear "tap for sound" indicator.

### Infinite Scroll
- Use `useInfiniteQuery` (TanStack React Query) for paginated feed loading.
- Pre-fetch the next page when the user is 2–3 items from the bottom.
- Show a subtle loading indicator (spinning icon or skeleton) during fetch — never a blank screen.
- Cache visited videos so back-navigation is instant.

