## 5. Responsive Layout Strategy

### Breakpoint Behavior

| Breakpoint | Layout | Content |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **Mobile** (< 768px) | Single column, full-screen video feed | Videos at 100dvh, bottom tab navigation |
| **Tablet** (768–1024px) | Single column with wider action bar | Videos maintain 9:16 aspect ratio centered |
| **Desktop** (> 1024px) | Multi-column: sidebar + video feed + suggestions | Videos in center column, sidebar for navigation |

**Rules:**
- Navigation: Bottom tab bar on mobile → Left sidebar on desktop.
- Video player: Full-bleed on mobile → Centered with max-width on desktop.
- Comment panel: Bottom sheet on mobile → Right sidebar panel on desktop.
- Never show horizontal scroll on any viewport.

---

## 6. Accessibility (A11y)

### Rules:
- All interactive elements must have `aria-label` or visible text labels.
- Video player controls must be keyboard-accessible (Space = play/pause, Arrow keys = seek, M = mute).
- Provide **captions/subtitles** support for video content. Design for "silent consumption" — many users watch without audio.
- Color alone must never convey meaning. Use icons + color + text together.
- Focus indicators must be visible and follow a logical tab order.
- Use `role="button"` on non-button clickable elements. Prefer semantic `<button>` elements.
- All images and decorative icons must have appropriate `alt` text or `aria-hidden="true"`.

---

## 7. Loading States & Error Handling UX

### Skeleton Loaders
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — Skeleton that matches the real content layout
<div className="animate-pulse space-y-3">
  <div className="h-full w-full bg-muted rounded" />         {/* Video placeholder */}
  <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
    <div className="h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-muted" />      {/* Avatar */}
    <div className="h-4 w-32 bg-muted rounded" />            {/* Username */}
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ WRONG — Generic spinner that doesn't match content shape
<div className="flex justify-center"><Spinner /></div>
```

**Rules:**
- Skeleton loaders must **mirror the exact layout** of the content they replace. Users should feel the content "painting in."
- Use `Suspense` boundaries at the page/section level with skeleton fallbacks.
- Empty states (no posts, no comments, no results) must have an illustration + clear message + CTA (e.g., "Be the first to comment").
- Error states must be friendly, not technical. "Something went wrong" + "Try again" button. Use `sonner` toasts for transient errors.

---

## 8. Optimistic UI & Perceived Performance

### Rules:
- **Like/Unlike**: Update the UI immediately. Revert on error.
- **Follow/Unfollow**: Update the button state and follower count immediately.
- **Comment Post**: Insert the comment into the list immediately with a "sending" indicator. Replace with confirmed comment on success.
- **Post Delete**: Remove from feed immediately. Show undo toast for 5 seconds.
- Navigation between tabs should feel **instant** — pre-fetch data for likely next destinations.

---

## 9. Design Don'ts (Anti-Patterns)

| ❌ Don't | ✅ Do Instead |
|:---|:---|
| Use raw browser fonts (Times New Roman, serif) | Use `next/font` with Inter, Roboto, or system-ui stack |
| Show a blank white page while loading | Show skeleton loaders that match content layout |
| Use generic red/blue/green for UI elements | Use curated semantic color tokens from design system |
| Put critical actions below the fold on mobile | Keep primary actions within thumb-reach zone |
| Block the entire page for a single failed request | Show inline error with retry button |
| Auto-play video with sound on first visit | Mute by default, show "tap for sound" indicator |
| Use `alert()` or `confirm()` for user interactions | Use `AlertDialog` from shadcn/ui or `sonner` toasts |
| Show raw API error messages to users | Map errors to user-friendly messages via i18n |
